<?php

return [
    // Overview
    'Web cache poisoning' => 'Web cache poisoning',
    "In this section, we'll talk about what web cache poisoning is and what behaviors can lead to web cache poisoning vulnerabilities. We'll also look at some ways of exploiting these vulnerabilities and suggest ways you can reduce your exposure to them." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas apa itu web cache poisoning, pola perilaku yang memicunya, cara eksploitasinya, dan langkah pencegahannya.',
    'What is web cache poisoning?' => 'Apa itu web cache poisoning?',
    'Web cache poisoning is an advanced technique whereby an attacker exploits the behavior of a web server and cache so that a harmful HTTP response is served to other users.' => 'Web cache poisoning adalah teknik lanjutan yang memanfaatkan perilaku server web dan cache agar respons HTTP berbahaya tersimpan lalu disajikan ke pengguna lain.',
    'Fundamentally, web cache poisoning involves two phases. First, the attacker must work out how to elicit a response from the back-end server that inadvertently contains some kind of dangerous payload. Once successful, they need to make sure that their response is cached and subsequently served to the intended victims.' => 'Serangan ini terdiri atas dua fase: memicu respons berbahaya dari back-end lewat input tak di-key, lalu memastikan respons tersebut tersimpan di cache bagi korban.',
    'A poisoned web cache can potentially be a devastating means of distributing numerous different attacks, exploiting vulnerabilities such as XSS, JavaScript injection, open redirection, and so on.' => 'Cache yang teracuni menjadi jalur distribusi massal untuk serangan seperti XSS, injeksi JavaScript, dan open redirection.',
    "If you're already familiar with the basic concepts behind web cache poisoning and just want to practice exploiting them on some realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets, you can access all of the labs in this topic from the link below." => 'Jika Anda sudah memahami konsep dasar web cache poisoning dan ingin berlatih eksploitasi pada target realistis, akses semua lab topik ini lewat tautan di bawah.',
    'View all web cache poisoning labs' => 'Lihat semua lab web cache poisoning',
    'Web cache poisoning research' => 'Riset web cache poisoning',
    'This technique was first popularized by our 2018 research paper, "Practical Web Cache Poisoning", and developed further in 2020 with a second research paper, "Web Cache Entanglement: Novel Pathways to Poisoning". If you\'re interested in a detailed description of how we discovered and exploited these vulnerabilities in the wild, the full write-ups are available on our research page.' => 'Teknik ini dipopulerkan lewat makalah riset "Practical Web Cache Poisoning" (2018) dan diperluas lewat "Web Cache Entanglement" (2020).',
    'Practical Web Cache Poisoning' => 'Practical Web Cache Poisoning',
    'Web Cache Entanglement: Novel Pathways to Poisoning' => 'Web Cache Entanglement: Novel Pathways to Poisoning',
    'How does a web cache work?' => 'Bagaimana cara kerja web cache?',
    'To understand how web cache poisoning vulnerabilities arise, it is important to have a basic understanding of how web caches work.' => 'Memahami cara kerja cache web merupakan syarat penting sebelum memburu celah web cache poisoning.',
    'If a server had to send a new response to every single HTTP request separately, this would likely overload the server, resulting in latency issues and a poor user experience, especially during busy periods. Caching is primarily a means of reducing such issues.' => 'Caching mengurangi beban server dan latensi dengan menyimpan salinan respons untuk disajikan ulang pada permintaan serupa.',
    "The cache sits between the server and the user, where it saves (caches) the responses to particular requests, usually for a fixed amount of time. If another user then sends an equivalent request, the cache simply serves a copy of the cached response directly to the user, without any interaction from the back-end. This greatly eases the load on the server by reducing the number of duplicate requests it has to handle." => 'Cache berada di antara pengguna dan server asal untuk melayani permintaan berulang tanpa membebani back-end.',
    'Cache keys' => 'Cache key',
    'When the cache receives an HTTP request, it first has to determine whether there is a cached response that it can serve directly, or whether it has to forward the request for handling by the back-end server. Caches identify equivalent requests by comparing a predefined subset of the request\'s components, known collectively as the "cache key". Typically, this would contain the request line and [[C0]] header. Components of the request that are not included in the cache key are said to be "unkeyed".' => 'Cache menilai kesamaan permintaan melalui sebagian elemen bernama "cache key" (lazimnya baris permintaan dan header [[C0]]). Elemen di luar cache key disebut unkeyed.',
    'If the cache key of an incoming request matches the key of a previous request, then the cache considers them to be equivalent. As a result, it will serve a copy of the cached response that was generated for the original request. This applies to all subsequent requests with the matching cache key, until the cached response expires.' => 'Jika cache key permintaan baru cocok dengan entri cache yang belum kedaluwarsa, respons tersimpan langsung diberikan.',
    "Crucially, the other components of the request are ignored altogether by the cache. We'll explore the impact of this behavior in more detail later." => 'Semua elemen unkeyed diabaikan saat pencarian cache, tetapi tetap diteruskan ke server back-end saat cache miss.',
    'What is the impact of a web cache poisoning attack?' => 'Apa dampak serangan web cache poisoning?',
    'The impact of web cache poisoning is heavily dependent on two key factors:' => 'Besarnya dampak serangan ini ditentukan oleh dua faktor utama:',
    '<strong>What exactly the attacker can successfully get cached</strong><br> As the poisoned cache is more a means of distribution than a standalone attack, the impact of web cache poisoning is inextricably linked to how harmful the injected payload is. As with most kinds of attack, web cache poisoning can also be used in combination with other attacks to escalate the potential impact even further.' => '<strong>Jenis payload yang berhasil masuk ke cache</strong><br>Seberapa berbahaya serangan yang didistribusikan (misalnya XSS di skrip global vs defacement kecil).',
    '<strong>The amount of traffic on the affected page</strong><br> The poisoned response will only be served to users who visit the affected page while the cache is poisoned. As a result, the impact can range from non-existent to massive depending on whether the page is popular or not. If an attacker managed to poison a cached response on the home page of a major website, for example, the attack could affect thousands of users without any subsequent interaction from the attacker.' => '<strong>Volume trafik halaman target</strong><br>Makin ramai halaman yang diracuni (seperti beranda atau aset bersama), makin banyak korban terdampak otomatis.',
    'Note that the duration of a cache entry doesn\'t necessarily affect the impact of web cache poisoning. An attack can usually be scripted in such a way that it re-poisons the cache indefinitely.' => 'Masa hidup cache yang singkat sekalipun bisa diakali dengan mengotomatiskan pengiriman ulang payload sebelum cache kedaluwarsa.',
    'Constructing a web cache poisoning attack' => 'Menyusun serangan web cache poisoning',
    'Generally speaking, constructing a basic web cache poisoning attack involves the following steps:' => 'Secara umum, penyusunan web cache poisoning melewati tiga tahap berikut:',
    '[[A0]]Identify and evaluate unkeyed inputs[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Identifikasi dan evaluasi input unkeyed[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]Elicit a harmful response from the back-end server[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Picu respons berbahaya dari back-end[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]Get the response cached[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Pastikan respons tersimpan di cache[[/A0]]',
    'Identify and evaluate unkeyed inputs' => 'Identifikasi dan evaluasi input unkeyed',
    'Any web cache poisoning attack relies on manipulation of unkeyed inputs, such as headers. Web caches ignore unkeyed inputs when deciding whether to serve a cached response to the user. This behavior means that you can use them to inject your payload and elicit a "poisoned" response which, if cached, will be served to all users whose requests have the matching cache key. Therefore, the first step when constructing a web cache poisoning attack is identifying unkeyed inputs that are supported by the server.' => 'Cari input di luar cache key (seperti header tambahan) yang tetap diproses aplikasi back-end.',
    'You can identify unkeyed inputs manually by adding random inputs to requests and observing whether or not they have an effect on the response. This can be obvious, such as reflecting the input in the response directly, or triggering an entirely different response. However, sometimes the effects are more subtle and require a bit of detective work to figure out. You can use tools such as Burp Comparer to compare the response with and without the injected input, but this still involves a significant amount of manual effort.' => 'Anda bisa menambah header uji secara manual dan membandingkan perbedaan responsnya, atau mengotomatiskan pencarian dengan ekstensi.',
    'Param Miner' => 'Param Miner',
    'Fortunately, you can automate the process of identifying unkeyed inputs by adding the [[A0]]Param Miner[[/A0]] extension to Burp from the BApp store. To use Param Miner, you simply right-click on a request that you want to investigate and click "Guess headers". Param Miner then runs in the background, sending requests containing different inputs from its extensive, built-in list of headers. If a request containing one of its injected inputs has an effect on the response, Param Miner logs this in Burp, either in the "Issues" pane if you are using Burp Suite Professional, or in the "Output" tab of the extension ("Extensions" &gt; "Installed" &gt; "Param Miner" &gt; "Output") if you are using Burp Suite Community Edition.' => 'Ekstensi seperti [[A0]]Param Miner[[/A0]] menguji ratusan nama header secara otomatis dengan cache buster agar aman.',
    'For example, in the following screenshot, Param Miner found an unkeyed header [[C0]] on the home page of the website:' => 'Contoh penemuan header unkeyed [[C0]] oleh alat penebak header:',
    '<strong>Caution:</strong> When testing for unkeyed inputs on a live website, there is a risk of inadvertently causing the cache to serve your generated responses to real users. Therefore, it is important to make sure that your requests all have a unique cache key so that they will only be served to you. To do this, you can manually add a cache buster (such as a unique parameter) to the request line each time you make a request. Alternatively, if you are using Param Miner, there are options for automatically adding a cache buster to every request.' => '<strong>Peringatan:</strong> Selalu sertakan parameter cache buster unik saat menguji situs produksi agar respons uji tidak tersaji ke pengguna sungguhan.',
    'Elicit a harmful response from the back-end server' => 'Picu respons berbahaya dari server back-end',
    'Once you have identified an unkeyed input, the next step is to evaluate exactly how the website processes it. Understanding this is essential to successfully eliciting a harmful response. If an input is reflected in the response from the server without being properly sanitized, or is used to dynamically generate other data, then this is a potential entry point for web cache poisoning.' => 'Amati cara aplikasi memproses header atau input tersebut untuk menemukan celah seperti refleksi XSS atau pengalihan URL skrip.',
    'Get the response cached' => 'Pastikan respons tersimpan di cache',
    'Manipulating inputs to elicit a harmful response is half the battle, but it doesn\'t achieve much unless you can cause the response to be cached, which can sometimes be tricky.' => 'Payload baru berdampak lintas pengguna jika respons berbahayanya benar-benar masuk ke cache.',
    'Whether or not a response gets cached can depend on all kinds of factors, such as the file extension, content type, route, status code, and response headers. You will probably need to devote some time to simply playing around with requests on different pages and studying how the cache behaves. Once you work out how to get a response cached that contains your malicious input, you are ready to deliver the exploit to potential victims.' => 'Perilaku caching bergantung pada rute, tipe konten, ekstensi, kode status, dan header Cache-Control/Age.',
    'Exploiting web cache poisoning vulnerabilities' => 'Mengeksploitasi kerentanan web cache poisoning',
    'This basic process can be used to discover and exploit a variety of different web cache poisoning vulnerabilities.' => 'Alur dasar ini dapat diterapkan pada berbagai jenis celah desain maupun implementasi cache.',
    'In some cases, web cache poisoning vulnerabilities arise due to general flaws in the design of caches. Other times, the way in which a cache is implemented by a specific website can introduce unexpected quirks that can be exploited.' => 'Celah dapat berasal dari kelemahan desain umum ataupun keunikan implementasi parser cache tertentu.',
    "In the following sections, we'll outline some of the most common examples of both of these scenarios. We've also provided a number of interactive labs so that you can see some of these vulnerabilities in action and practice exploiting them." => 'Dua halaman berikut mengupas contoh nyata kedua skenario tersebut bersama lab praktiknya.',
    'Exploiting cache design flaws' => 'Mengeksploitasi cacat desain cache',
    'Exploiting cache implementation flaws' => 'Mengeksploitasi cacat implementasi cache',
    'How to prevent web cache poisoning vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan web cache poisoning',
    'The definitive way to prevent web cache poisoning would clearly be to disable caching altogether. While for many websites this might not be a realistic option, in other cases, it might be feasible. For example, if you only use caching because it was switched on by default when you adopted a CDN, it might be worth evaluating whether the default caching options really do reflect your needs.' => 'Jika tidak benar-benar dibutuhkan, nonaktifkan caching pada halaman dinamis dan tinjau aturan bawaan CDN.',
    'Even if you do need to use caching, restricting it to purely static responses is also effective, provided you are sufficiently wary about what you class as "static". For instance, make sure that an attacker can\'t trick the back-end server into retrieving their malicious version of a static resource instead of the genuine one.' => 'Batasi caching hanya untuk aset statis murni yang tidak bergantung pada header atau parameter dinamis klien.',
    "This is also related to a wider point about web security. Most websites now incorporate a variety of third-party technologies into both their development processes and day-to-day operations. No matter how robust your own internal security posture may be, as soon as you incorporate third-party technology into your environment, you are relying on its developers also being as security-conscious as you are. On the basis that you are only as secure as your weakest point, it is vital to make sure that you fully understand the security implications of any third-party technology before you integrate it." => 'Pahami implikasi keamanan tiap komponen pihak ketiga atau CDN yang dipasang di depan aplikasi.',
    "Specifically in the context of web cache poisoning, this not only means deciding whether to leave caching switched on by default, but also looking at which headers are supported by your CDN, for example. Several of the web cache poisoning vulnerabilities discussed above are exposed because an attacker is able to manipulate a series of obscure request headers, many of which are entirely unnecessary for the website's functionality. Again, you may be exposing yourself to these kinds of attacks without realizing, purely because you have implemented some technology that supports these unkeyed inputs by default. If a header isn't needed for the site to work, then it should be disabled." => 'Nonaktifkan dukungan header tak terpakai seperti X-Forwarded-Host jika tidak diperlukan aplikasi.',
    'You should also take the following precautions when implementing caching:' => 'Tambahan langkah pengamanan saat menerapkan cache:',
    'If you are considering excluding something from the cache key for performance reasons, rewrite the request instead.' => 'Jika mengabaikan suatu parameter dari cache key demi performa, tulis ulang/hapus parameter tersebut sebelum diteruskan ke back-end.',
    'Don\'t accept fat [[C0]] requests. Be aware that some third-party technologies may permit this by default.' => 'Tolak permintaan fat [[C0]] yang menyertakan body.',
    'Patch client-side vulnerabilities even if they seem unexploitable. Some of these vulnerabilities might actually be exploitable due to unpredictable quirks in your cache\'s behavior. It could be a matter of time before someone finds a quirk, whether it be cache-based or otherwise, that makes this vulnerability exploitable.' => 'Tetap tambal kerentanan sisi klien yang tampak sulit dieksploitasi karena keunikan cache bisa menjadikannya eksploitabel.',

    // exploiting-design-flaws
    "In this section, we'll look more closely at how web cache poisoning vulnerabilities can arise due to general flaws in the design of caches. We'll also demonstrate how these can be exploited." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menelaah celah web cache poisoning yang lahir dari kelemahan desain cache beserta cara eksploitasinya.',
    'In short, websites are vulnerable to web cache poisoning if they handle unkeyed input in an unsafe way and allow the subsequent HTTP responses to be cached. This vulnerability can be used as a delivery method for a variety of different attacks.' => 'Intinya, aplikasi rentan saat memproses input unkeyed secara tidak aman di dalam respons yang diizinkan masuk cache.',
    'Using web cache poisoning to deliver an XSS attack' => 'Memakai web cache poisoning untuk mengirim serangan XSS',
    'Perhaps the simplest web cache poisoning vulnerability to exploit is when unkeyed input is reflected in a cacheable response without proper sanitization.' => 'Kasus paling sederhana adalah refleksi header unkeyed tanpa sanitasi di halaman yang di-cache.',
    'For example, consider the following request and response:' => 'Perhatikan contoh permintaan dan respons berikut:',
    'Here, the value of the [[C0]] header is being used to dynamically generate an Open Graph image URL, which is then reflected in the response. Crucially for web cache poisoning, the [[C1]] header is often unkeyed. In this example, the cache can potentially be poisoned with a response containing a simple XSS payload:' => 'Header [[C0]] (yang umumnya unkeyed di [[C1]] pada cache) dipakai membentuk tag meta sehingga bisa disuntikkan payload XSS:',
    "If this response was cached, all users who accessed [[C0]] would be served this XSS payload. This example simply causes an alert to appear in the victim's browser, but a real attack could potentially steal passwords and hijack user accounts." => 'Jika masuk ke cache, setiap pengunjung halaman [[C0]] otomatis mengeksekusi payload XSS tersebut.',
    'Exploiting cross-site scripting vulnerabilities' => 'Mengeksploitasi kerentanan cross-site scripting',
    'Using web cache poisoning to exploit unsafe handling of resource imports' => 'Memanfaatkan cache poisoning pada pemuatan sumber daya eksternal',
    'Some websites use unkeyed headers to dynamically generate URLs for importing resources, such as externally hosted JavaScript files. In this case, if an attacker changes the value of the appropriate header to a domain that they control, they could potentially manipulate the URL to point to their own malicious JavaScript file instead.' => 'Jika header unkeyed menentukan host pada tag script atau impor aset, penyerang dapat mengarahkannya ke server miliknya sendiri.',
    "If the response containing this malicious URL is cached, the attacker's JavaScript file would be imported and executed in the browser session of any user whose request has a matching cache key." => 'Begitu responsnya tersimpan di cache, semua pengguna dengan cache key sama akan mengunduh skrip berbahaya penyerang.',
    'Using web cache poisoning to exploit cookie-handling vulnerabilities' => 'Memanfaatkan cache poisoning pada penanganan cookie yang lemah',
    'Cookies are often used to dynamically generate content in a response. A common example might be a cookie that indicates the user\'s preferred language, which is then used to load the corresponding version of the page:' => 'Cookie seperti pengatur bahasa halaman sering ikut menentukan respons server padahal tidak masuk cache key:',
    "In this example, the Polish version of a blog post is being requested. Notice that the information about which language version to serve is only contained in the [[C0]] header. Let's suppose that the cache key contains the request line and the [[C1]] header, but not the [[C2]] header. In this case, if the response to this request is cached, then all subsequent users who tried to access this blog post would receive the Polish version as well, regardless of which language they actually selected." => 'Jika [[C0]] dan [[C2]] tidak masuk cache key (hanya baris permintaan dan [[C1]]), respons berisi injeksi atau preferensi lewat cookie dapat diracuni ke semua pengunjung.',
    'This flawed handling of cookies by the cache can also be exploited using web cache poisoning techniques. In practice, however, this vector is relatively rare in comparison to header-based cache poisoning. When cookie-based cache poisoning vulnerabilities exist, they tend to be identified and resolved quickly because legitimate users have accidentally poisoned the cache.' => 'Jika cookie yang terpantul tidak disanitasi (XSS), dampaknya langsung menjangkau seluruh pengguna.',
    'Using multiple headers to exploit web cache poisoning vulnerabilities' => 'Menggunakan beberapa header sekaligus untuk eksploitasi',
    'Some websites are vulnerable to simple web cache poisoning exploits, as demonstrated above. However, others require more sophisticated attacks and only become vulnerable when an attacker is able to craft a request that manipulates multiple unkeyed inputs.' => 'Terkadang celah baru dapat dieksploitasi dengan memadukan beberapa header unkeyed secara bersamaan.',
    'For example, let\'s say a website requires secure communication using HTTPS. To enforce this, if a request that uses another protocol is received, the website dynamically generates a redirect to itself that does use HTTPS:' => 'Misalnya header protokol memicu pengalihan HTTPS yang juga membaca host dari header unkeyed lain:',
    'By itself, this behavior isn\'t necessarily vulnerable. However, by combining this with what we learned earlier about vulnerabilities in dynamically generated URLs, an attacker could potentially exploit this behavior to generate a cacheable response that redirects users to a malicious URL.' => 'Kombinasi dua header unkeyed ini dapat menghasilkan respons redirect ter-cache menuju domain penyerang.',
    'Exploiting responses that expose too much information' => 'Memanfaatkan respons yang terlalu banyak mengungkap informasi',
    'Sometimes websites make themselves more vulnerable to web cache poisoning by giving away too much information about themselves and their behavior.' => 'Informasi diagnostik pada header respons mempermudah penyerang menyinkronkan waktu pengiriman payload.',
    'Cache-control directives' => 'Direktif Cache-Control',
    'One of the challenges when constructing a web cache poisoning attack is ensuring that the harmful response gets cached. This can involve a lot of manual trial and error to study how the cache behaves. However, sometimes responses explicitly reveal some of the information an attacker needs to successfully poison the cache.' => 'Header respons sering memberi tahu apakah respons disimpan dan berapa lama sisa umurnya di cache.',
    'One such example is when responses contain information about how often the cache is purged or how old the currently cached response is:' => 'Contoh header respons yang mengungkap usia dan masa berlaku cache:',
    'Although this doesn\'t directly lead to web cache poisoning vulnerabilities, it does save a potential attacker some of the manual effort involved because they know exactly when to send their payload to ensure it gets cached.' => 'Nilai Age dan max-age memberi waktu tepat kapan cache akan kedaluwarsa.',
    'This knowledge also enables far more subtle attacks. Rather than bombarding the back-end server with requests until one sticks, which could raise suspicions, the attacker can carefully time a single malicious request to poison the cache.' => 'Penyerang cukup mengirim satu permintaan tepat pada detik cache kadaluwarsa.',
    'Vary header' => 'Header Vary',
    'The rudimentary way that the [[C0]] header is often used can also provide attackers with a helping hand. The [[C1]] header specifies a list of additional headers that should be treated as part of the cache key even if they are normally unkeyed. It is commonly used to specify that the [[C2]] header is keyed, for example, so that if the mobile version of a website is cached, this won\'t be served to non-mobile users by mistake.' => 'Header [[C0]] mencantumkan header tambahan yang ikut di-key oleh cache (seperti [[C2]] di sebelah [[C1]]), yang bisa dibaca penyerang untuk menyasar kelompok pengguna tertentu.',
    'This information can also be used to construct a multi-step attack to target a specific subset of users. For example, if the attacker knows that the [[C0]] header is part of the cache key, by first identifying the user agent of the intended victims, they could tailor the attack so that only users with that user agent are affected. Alternatively, they could work out which user agent was most commonly used to access the site, and tailor the attack to affect the maximum number of users that way.' => 'Dengan mengetahui nilai [[C0]] target, penyerang bisa menembak korban spesifik meskipun header tersebut masuk dalam cache key.',
    'Using web cache poisoning to exploit DOM-based vulnerabilities' => 'Menggunakan web cache poisoning untuk celah berbasis DOM',
    'As discussed earlier, if the website unsafely uses unkeyed headers to import files, this can potentially be exploited by an attacker to import a malicious file instead. However, this applies to more than just JavaScript files.' => 'Header unkeyed juga dapat mengalihkan impor berkas data seperti JSON ke server penyerang.',
    'Many websites use JavaScript to fetch and process additional data from the back-end. If a script handles data from the server in an unsafe way, this can potentially lead to all kinds of DOM-based vulnerabilities.' => 'Jika JavaScript halaman memproses JSON hasil impor ke sink berbahaya tanpa sanitasi, muncullah celah DOM-based.',
    'For example, an attacker could poison the cache with a response that imports a JSON file containing the following payload:' => 'Contoh payload JSON berbahaya yang dihidangkan server penyerang:',
    "If the website then passes the value of this property into a sink that supports dynamic code execution, the payload would be executed in the context of the victim's browser session." => 'Saat nilai properti masuk ke sink seperti innerHTML atau eval, skrip penyerang langsung berjalan di sesi korban.',
    'If you use web cache poisoning to make a website load malicious JSON data from your server, you may need to grant the website access to the JSON using CORS:' => 'Pastikan server Anda mengizinkan akses lintas origin via header CORS agar browser mau membacanya:',
    'DOM-based vulnerabilities' => 'Kerentanan berbasis DOM',
    'Chaining web cache poisoning vulnerabilities' => 'Merangkai kerentanan web cache poisoning',
    "As we saw earlier, sometimes an attacker is only able to elicit a malicious response by crafting a request using multiple headers. But the same is also true of different types of attack. Web cache poisoning sometimes requires the attacker to chain together several of the techniques we've discussed. By chaining together different vulnerabilities, it is often possible to expose additional layers of vulnerability that were initially unexploitable." => 'Menggabungkan beberapa teknik sekaligus seperti header redirect, CORS, dan celah DOM sering membuka rantai eksploitasi bernilai tinggi.',

    // exploiting-implementation-flaws
    'Exploiting cache implementation flaws' => 'Mengeksploitasi cacat implementasi cache',
    'In our previous labs, you learned how to exploit web cache poisoning vulnerabilities by manipulating typical unkeyed inputs, such as HTTP headers and cookies. While this approach is effective, it only scratches the surface of what is possible with web cache poisoning.' => 'Selain header dan cookie unkeyed biasa, keunikan implementasi cache key membuka vektor serangan yang jauh lebih luas.',
    "In this section, we'll demonstrate how you can access a much greater attack surface for web cache poisoning by exploiting quirks in specific implementations of caching systems. In particular, we'll look at why flaws in how cache keys are generated can sometimes leave websites vulnerable to cache poisoning via separate vulnerabilities that are traditionally considered unexploitable. We'll also show how you can take classic techniques even further to potentially poison application-level caches, often with devastating results." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menunjukkan bagaimana keanehan penyusunan cache key dan cache internal aplikasi dapat dieksploitasi.',
    'These techniques were first documented by our Director of Research, James Kettle, for his presentation "Web Cache Entanglement: Novel Pathways to Poisoning" at BlackHat USA 2020. If you\'re interested in seeing how he was able to discover and exploit these vulnerabilities in the wild, you can access a recording of this presentation, and the accompanying whitepaper, from our research page.' => 'Teknik-teknik ini didokumentasikan dalam riset "Web Cache Entanglement: Novel Pathways to Poisoning".',
    'Cache key flaws' => 'Cacat pada cache key',
    'Generally speaking, websites take most of their input from the URL path and the query string. As a result, this is a well-trodden attack surface for various hacking techniques. However, as the request line is usually part of the cache key, these inputs have traditionally not been considered suitable for cache poisoning. Any payload injected via keyed inputs would act as a cache buster, meaning your poisoned cache entry would almost certainly never be served to any other users.' => 'Lazimnya parameter URL ikut masuk cache key sehingga tak cocok untuk cache poisoning, kecuali jika ada transformasi tersembunyi.',
    'On closer inspection, however, the behavior of individual caching systems is not always as you would expect. In practice, many websites and CDNs perform various transformations on keyed components when they are saved in the cache key. This can include:' => 'Banyak sistem cache dan CDN memodifikasi komponen keyed saat menyimpannya, antara lain:',
    'Excluding the query string' => 'Mengabaikan seluruh query string',
    'Filtering out specific query parameters' => 'Menghapus parameter query tertentu',
    'Normalizing input in keyed components' => 'Menormalisasi nilai di komponen keyed',
    'These transformations may introduce a few unexpected quirks. These are primarily based around discrepancies between the data that is written to the cache key and the data that is passed into the application code, even though it all stems from the same input. These cache key flaws can be exploited to poison the cache via inputs that may initially appear unusable.' => 'Selisih antara nilai yang dipakai membangun cache key dan nilai yang diteruskan ke aplikasi inilah sumber celahnya.',
    'In the case of fully integrated, application-level caches, these quirks can be even more extreme. In fact, internal caches can be so unpredictable that it is sometimes difficult to test them at all without inadvertently poisoning the cache for live users.' => 'Pada cache terintegrasi di level aplikasi, perilakunya sering tidak mengenal cache buster sama sekali.',
    'Cache probing methodology' => 'Metodologi penyelidikan cache',
    'The methodology of probing for cache implementation flaws differs slightly from the classic web cache poisoning methodology. These newer techniques rely on flaws in the specific implementation and configuration of the cache, which may vary dramatically from site to site. This means that you need a deeper understanding of the target cache and its behavior.' => 'Karena perilaku implementasi berbeda di tiap target, dibutuhkan penyelidikan sistematis untuk memahami logika cache.',
    "In this section, we'll outline the high-level methodology for probing the cache to understand its behavior and identify any potential flaws. Afterwards, we'll provide some more concrete examples of common cache key flaws and how you can exploit them." => 'Berikut tiga tahap metodologi penggalian cacat cache.',
    'The methodology involves the following steps:' => 'Tahapan penyelidikannya meliputi:',
    '[[A0]]Identify a suitable cache oracle[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Temukan cache oracle yang tepat[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]Probe key handling[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Uji penanganan cache key[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]Identify an exploitable gadget[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Temukan gadget untuk dieksploitasi[[/A0]]',
    'Identify a suitable cache oracle' => 'Temukan cache oracle yang sesuai',
    "The first step is to identify a suitable \"cache oracle\" that you can use for testing. A cache oracle is simply a page or endpoint that provides feedback about the cache's behavior. This needs to be cacheable and must indicate in some way whether you received a cached response or a response directly from the server. This feedback could take various forms, such as:" => 'Cache oracle adalah endpoint yang dapat di-cache sekaligus memberi sinyal apakah balasan berasal dari cache atau server asal, seperti:',
    'An HTTP header that explicitly tells you whether you got a cache hit' => 'Header HTTP penanda hit atau miss',
    'Observable changes to dynamic content' => 'Perubahan nyata pada konten dinamis atau stempel waktu',
    'Distinct response times' => 'Perbedaan waktu respons yang terukur',
    'Ideally, the cache oracle will also reflect the entire URL and at least one query parameter in the response. This will make it easier to notice parsing discrepancies between the cache and the application, which will be useful for constructing different exploits later.' => 'Idealnya halaman tersebut juga memantulkan URL dan parameter query di respons.',
    'If you can identify that a specific third-party cache is being used, you can also consult the corresponding documentation. This may contain information about how the default cache key is constructed. You might even stumble across some handy tips and tricks, such as features that allow you to see the cache key directly. For example, Akamai-based websites may support the header [[C0]], which you can use to display the cache key in the response headers:' => 'Beberapa layanan CDN bahkan menyediakan header diagnostik untuk mencetak cache key secara langsung seperti [[C0]]:',
    'Probe key handling' => 'Uji penanganan cache key',
    'The next step is to investigate whether the cache performs any additional processing of your input when generating the cache key. You are looking for an additional attack surface hidden within seemingly keyed components.' => 'Uji apakah ada bagian dari komponen keyed yang dibuang atau dinormalisasi sebelum dijadikan kunci.',
    'You should specifically look at any transformation that is taking place. Is anything being excluded from a keyed component when it is added to the cache key? Common examples are excluding specific query parameters, or even the entire query string, and removing the port from the [[C0]] header.' => 'Misalnya pembuangan parameter query, query string penuh, atau angka port pada header [[C0]].',
    'If you\'re fortunate enough to have direct access to the cache key, you can simply compare the key after injecting different inputs. Otherwise, you can use your understanding of the cache oracle to infer whether you received the correct cached response. For each case that you want to test, you send two similar requests and compare the responses.' => 'Kirim sepasang permintaan uji lalu bandingkan apakah permintaan kedua mendapat cache hit dari permintaan pertama.',
    'Let\'s say that our hypothetical cache oracle is the target website\'s home page. This automatically redirects users to a region-specific page. It uses the [[C0]] header to dynamically generate the [[C1]] header in the response:' => 'Contoh pengujian port pada header [[C0]] yang memengaruhi header [[C1]]:',
    'To test whether the port is excluded from the cache key, we first need to request an arbitrary port and make sure that we receive a fresh response from the server that reflects this input:' => 'Kirim permintaan pertama dengan nomor port kustom saat cache miss:',
    'Next, we\'ll send another request, but this time we won\'t specify a port:' => 'Lalu kirim permintaan kedua tanpa nomor port:',
    'As you can see, we have been served our cached response even though the [[C0]] header in the request does not specify a port. This proves that the port is being excluded from the cache key. Importantly, the full header is still passed into the application code and reflected in the response.' => 'Permintaan tanpa port ternyata menerima balasan ter-cache berisi port buatan tadi, membuktikan port dibuang dari cache key namun tetap diteruskan ke back-end [[C0]].',
    'In short, although the [[C0]] header is keyed, the way it is transformed by the cache allows us to pass a payload into the application while still preserving a "normal" cache key that will be mapped to other users\' requests. This kind of behavior is the key concept behind all of the exploits that we\'ll discuss in this section.' => 'Dengan begitu, payload masuk lewat [[C0]] sementara cache key tetap tampak normal bagi pengunjung lain.',
    'You can use a similar approach to investigate any other processing of your input by the cache. Is your input being normalized in any way? How is your input stored? Do you notice any anomalies? We\'ll cover how to answer these questions later using concrete examples.' => 'Terapkan pengujian berpasangan serupa untuk mengecek normalisasi URL dan perlakuan delimiter.',
    'Identify an exploitable gadget' => 'Temukan gadget yang dapat dieksploitasi',
    "By now, you should have a relatively solid understanding of how the target website's cache behaves and might have found some interesting flaws in the way the cache key is constructed. The final step is to identify a suitable gadget that you can chain with this cache key flaw. This is an important skill because the severity of any web cache poisoning attack is heavily dependent on the gadget you are able to exploit." => 'Setelah memahami cacat cache key, cari gadget di aplikasi (seperti XSS, open redirect, atau pengubah resource) untuk dirangkai.',
    'These gadgets will often be classic client-side vulnerabilities, such as reflected XSS and open redirects. By combining these with web cache poisoning, you can massively escalate the severity of these attacks, turning a reflected vulnerability into a stored one. Instead of having to induce a victim to visit a specially crafted URL, your payload will automatically be served to anybody who visits the ordinary, perfectly legitimate URL.' => 'Penggabungan ini menaikkan celah reflected biasa menjadi serangan stored persisten tanpa butuh pancingan tautan ke korban.',
    'Perhaps even more interestingly, these techniques enable you to exploit a number of unclassified vulnerabilities that are often dismissed as "unexploitable" and left unpatched. This includes the use of dynamic content in resource files, and exploits requiring malformed requests that a browser would never send.' => 'Bahkan bug yang mustahil dikirim browser langsung kini bisa disalurkan lewat cache.',
    'Exploiting cache key flaws' => 'Mengeksploitasi cacat cache key',
    "Now that you're familiar with the high-level methodology, let's take a look at some typical cache key flaws and how you might exploit them. We'll cover:" => 'Berikut ragam cacat cache key yang umum ditemui:',
    '[[A0]]Unkeyed port[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Port unkeyed[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]Unkeyed query string[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Query string unkeyed[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Unkeyed query parameters[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Parameter query unkeyed[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Cache parameter cloaking[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Parameter cloaking pada cache[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Normalized cache keys[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Normalisasi cache key[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Cache key injection[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Injeksi cache key[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Internal cache poisoning[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Cache poisoning internal[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    'Unkeyed port' => 'Port unkeyed',
    'The [[C0]] header is often part of the cache key and, as such, initially seems an unlikely candidate for injecting any kind of payload. However, some caching systems will parse the header and exclude the port from the cache key.' => 'Meski header [[C0]] masuk cache key, sebagian cache membuang angka port-nya saat membangun kunci.',
    'In this case, you can potentially use this header for web cache poisoning. For example, consider the case we saw earlier where a redirect URL was dynamically generated based on the [[C0]] header. This might enable you to construct a denial-of-service attack by simply adding an arbitrary port to the request. All users who browsed to the home page would be redirected to a dud port, effectively taking down the home page until the cache expired.' => 'Jika [[C0]] dipakai ulang untuk membentuk redirect atau URL skrip, penambahan port palsu dapat memicu DoS maupun XSS.',
    'This kind of attack can be escalated further if the website allows you to specify a non-numeric port. You could use this to inject an XSS payload, for example.' => 'Jika server mengizinkan port non-numerik, penyerang bahkan bisa menyuntikkan payload XSS.',
    'Unkeyed query string' => 'Query string unkeyed',
    'Like the [[C0]] header, the request line is typically keyed. However, one of the most common cache-key transformations is to exclude the entire query string.' => 'Banyak konfigurasi cache mengabaikan seluruh query string saat membuat kunci demi meningkatkan rasio cache hit meski [[C0]] dan path di-key.',
    'Detecting an unkeyed query string' => 'Mendeteksi query string unkeyed',
    'If the response explicitly tells you whether you got a cache hit or not, this transformation is relatively simple to spot - but what if it doesn\'t? This has the side-effect of making dynamic pages appear as though they are fully static because it can be hard to know whether you are communicating with the cache or the server.' => 'Jika query string diabaikan dari cache key, perubahan parameter URL tetap mengembalikan respons cache yang sama.',
    'To identify a dynamic page, you would normally observe how changing a parameter value has an effect on the response. But if the query string is unkeyed, most of the time you would still get a cache hit, and therefore an unchanged response, regardless of any parameters you add. Clearly, this also makes classic cache-buster query parameters redundant.' => 'Akibatnya cache buster di query string menjadi tidak mempan.',
    'Fortunately, there are alternative ways of adding a cache buster, such as adding it to a keyed header that doesn\'t interfere with the application\'s behavior. Some typical examples include:' => 'Sebagai ganti, taruh cache buster di dalam header yang ikut di-key seperti:',
    'If you use Param Miner, you can also select the options "Add static/dynamic cache buster" and "Include cache busters in headers". It will then automatically add a cache buster to commonly keyed headers in any requests that you send using Burp\'s manual testing tools.' => 'Anda juga dapat mengonfigurasi cache buster otomatis di dalam header.',
    'Another approach is to see whether there are any discrepancies between how the cache and the back-end normalize the path of the request. As the path is almost guaranteed to be keyed, you can sometimes exploit this to issue requests with different keys that still hit the same endpoint. For example, the following entries might all be cached separately but treated as equivalent to [[C0]] on the back-end:' => 'Cara lain adalah memanfaatkan variasi penulisan path yang mengarah ke [[C0]] tetapi dianggap cache key berbeda:',
    'Apache: [[C0]] Nginx: [[C1]] PHP: [[C2]] .NET [[C3]]' => 'Apache: [[C0]] Nginx: [[C1]] PHP: [[C2]] .NET: [[C3]]',
    'This transformation can sometimes mask what would otherwise be glaringly obvious reflected XSS vulnerabilities. If penetration testers or automated scanners only receive cached responses without realizing, it can appear as though there is no reflected XSS on the page.' => 'Pengujian yang tidak menyadari query string unkeyed bisa melewatkan celah reflected XSS yang sebenarnya nyata.',
    'Exploiting an unkeyed query string' => 'Mengeksploitasi query string unkeyed',
    'Excluding the query string from the cache key can actually make these reflected XSS vulnerabilities even more severe.' => 'Dengan mengecualikan query string, celah reflected XSS justru bisa diracuni ke cache agar berdampak pada pengunjung URL polos.',
    'Usually, such an attack would rely on inducing the victim to visit a maliciously crafted URL. However, poisoning the cache via an unkeyed query string would cause the payload to be served to users who visit what would otherwise be a perfectly normal URL. This has the potential to impact a far greater number of victims with no further interaction from the attacker.' => 'Siapa pun yang membuka URL normal tanpa query string akan langsung menerima respons XSS tersebut.',
    'Unkeyed query parameters' => 'Parameter query unkeyed',
    'So far we\'ve seen that on some websites, the entire query string is excluded from the cache key. But some websites only exclude specific query parameters that are not relevant to the back-end application, such as parameters for analytics or serving targeted advertisements. UTM parameters like [[C0]] are good candidates to check during testing.' => 'Sebagian cache hanya membuang parameter pelacakan tertentu seperti [[C0]] dari cache key.',
    'Parameters that have been excluded from the cache key are unlikely to have a significant impact on the response. The chances are there won\'t be any useful gadgets that accept input from these parameters. That said, some pages handle the entire URL in a vulnerable manner, making it possible to exploit arbitrary parameters.' => 'Jika halaman memantulkan seluruh URL lengkap atau query string, parameter yang dikecualikan tadi bisa dipakai meracuni cache.',
    'Cache parameter cloaking' => 'Parameter cloaking pada cache',
    "If the cache excludes a harmless parameter from the cache key, and you can't find any exploitable gadgets based on the full URL, you'd be forgiven for thinking that you've reached a dead end. However, this is actually where things can get interesting." => 'Meski parameter yang dikecualikan tak dipakai aplikasi, selisih parsing delimiter dapat memboncengkan parameter lain ke dalam aplikasi.',
    'If you can work out how the cache parses the URL to identify and remove the unwanted parameters, you might find some interesting quirks. Of particular interest are any parsing discrepancies between the cache and the application. This can potentially allow you to sneak arbitrary parameters into the application logic by "cloaking" them in an excluded parameter.' => 'Penyelundupan parameter terjadi ketika cache dan back-end memecah tanda pemisah query string secara berbeda.',
    'For example, the de facto standard is that a parameter will either be preceded by a question mark ([[C0]]), if it\'s the first one in the query string, or an ampersand ([[C1]]). Some poorly written parsing algorithms will treat any [[C2]] as the start of a new parameter, regardless of whether it\'s the first one or not.' => 'Misalnya cache menganggap [[C0]] maupun [[C2]] kedua sebagai awal parameter baru sedangkan back-end hanya mengakui [[C1]].',
    'Let\'s assume that the algorithm for excluding parameters from the cache key behaves in this way, but the server\'s algorithm only accepts the first [[C0]] as a delimiter. Consider the following request:' => 'Jika server hanya memakai [[C0]] pertama sebagai pemisah, lihat permintaan berikut:',
    'In this case, the cache would identify two parameters and exclude the second one from the cache key. However, the server doesn\'t accept the second [[C0]] as a delimiter and instead only sees one parameter, [[C1]], whose value is the entire rest of the query string, including our payload. If the value of [[C2]] is passed into a useful gadget, we have successfully injected our payload without affecting the cache key.' => 'Cache membuang bagian setelah [[C0]] kedua dari kunci, sedangkan server membaca keseluruhan sisa string sebagai nilai [[C1]] (dan [[C2]] membawa payload).',
    'Exploiting parameter parsing quirks' => 'Mengeksploitasi perbedaan parsing parameter',
    'Similar parameter cloaking issues can arise in the opposite scenario, where the back-end identifies distinct parameters that the cache does not. The Ruby on Rails framework, for example, interprets both ampersands (&) and semicolons (;) as delimiters. When used in conjunction with a cache that does not allow this, you can potentially exploit another quirk to override the value of a keyed parameter in the application logic.' => 'Di Ruby on Rails, karakter & dan ; sama-sama dianggap pemisah parameter sementara sebagian besar cache hanya memakai &.',
    'Consider the following request:' => 'Perhatikan permintaan berikut:',
    'As the names suggest, [[C0]] is included in the cache key, but [[C1]] is not. Many caches will only interpret this as two parameters, delimited by the ampersand:' => 'Cache hanya memecah pada ampersand sehingga [[C0]] bernilai normal dan [[C1]] memuat sisa parameter yang dibuang dari kunci:',
    'Once the parsing algorithm removes the [[C0]], the cache key will only contain [[C1]]. On the back-end, however, Ruby on Rails sees the semicolon and splits the query string into three separate parameters:' => 'Setelah [[C0]] dihapus, cache key tetap [[C1]]. Namun back-end memecah titik koma menjadi tiga parameter:',
    "But now there is a duplicate [[C0]]. This is where the second quirk comes into play. If there are duplicate parameters, each with different values, Ruby on Rails gives precedence to the final occurrence. The end result is that the cache key contains an innocent, expected parameter value, allowing the cached response to be served as normal to other users. On the back-end, however, the same parameter has a completely different value, which is our injected payload. It is this second value that will be passed into the gadget and reflected in the poisoned response." => 'Saat ada dua [[C0]] dengan nama sama, Ruby on Rails mengambil nilai yang paling akhir sehingga respons beracun tersimpan di cache key normal.',
    'This exploit can be especially powerful if it gives you control over a function that will be executed. For example, if a website is using JSONP to make a cross-domain request, this will often contain a [[C0]] parameter to execute a given function on the returned data:' => 'Hal ini sangat berbahaya pada endpoint JSONP yang memakai parameter [[C0]] untuk menentukan nama fungsi JavaScript:',
    'In this case, you could use these techniques to override the expected callback function and execute arbitrary JavaScript instead.' => 'Penyerang dapat menimpa nama fungsi callback menjadi kode JavaScript sembarang.',
    'Exploiting fat GET support' => 'Mengeksploitasi dukungan fat GET',
    'In select cases, the HTTP method may not be keyed. This might allow you to poison the cache with a [[C0]] request containing a malicious payload in the body. Your payload would then even be served in response to users\' [[C1]] requests. Although this scenario is pretty rare, you can sometimes achieve a similar effect by simply adding a body to a [[C2]] request to create a "fat" [[C3]] request:' => 'Ketika back-end membaca body pada permintaan [[C2]] ("fat" [[C3]] atau [[C0]]) sementara cache key hanya membaca baris permintaan [[C1]]:',
    'In this case, the cache key would be based on the request line, but the server-side value of the parameter would be taken from the body.' => 'Nilai parameter di query menjaga cache key bersih sementara nilai berbahaya di body diprioritaskan aplikasi.',
    'This is only possible if a website accepts [[C0]] requests that have a body, but there are potential workarounds. You can sometimes encourage "fat [[C1]]" handling by overriding the HTTP method, for example:' => 'Jika permintaan [[C0]] ber-body ditolak, coba pancing mode "fat [[C1]]" memakai header override metode HTTP:',
    'As long as the [[C0]] header is unkeyed, you could submit a pseudo-[[C1]] request while preserving a [[C2]] cache key derived from the request line.' => 'Selama [[C0]] bersifat unkeyed, Anda bisa mengirim [[C1]] semu dengan cache key [[C2]] normal.',
    'Exploiting dynamic content in resource imports' => 'Mengeksploitasi konten dinamis di aset impor',
    "Imported resource files are typically static but some reflect input from the query string. This is mostly considered harmless because browsers rarely execute these files when viewed directly, and an attacker has no control over the URLs used to load a page's subresources. However, by combining this with web cache poisoning, you can occasionally inject content into the resource file." => 'Berkas seperti CSS yang memantulkan query string dapat diracuni jika query parameter tersebut tidak di-key.',
    'For example, consider a page that reflects the current query string in an import statement:' => 'Misalnya halaman CSS memantulkan query string ke dalam aturan @import:',
    'You could exploit this behavior to inject malicious CSS that exfiltrates sensitive information from any pages that import [[C0]].' => 'Anda dapat menyuntikkan CSS berbahaya ke semua halaman yang mengimpor [[C0]].',
    'If the page importing the CSS file doesn\'t specify a [[C0]], you can maybe even exploit static CSS files. Given the right configuration, browsers will simply scour the document looking for CSS and then execute it. This means that you can occasionally poison static CSS files by triggering a server error that reflects the excluded query parameter:' => 'Jika halaman pengimpor tidak menetapkan [[C0]], respons galat yang memantulkan query string bahkan tetap dapat ditafsirkan browser sebagai aturan CSS:',
    'Normalized cache keys' => 'Cache key yang dinormalisasi',
    'Any normalization applied to the cache key can also introduce exploitable behavior. In fact, it can occasionally enable some exploits that would otherwise be almost impossible.' => 'Normalisasi pada cache key dapat menghidupkan kembali kerentanan XSS yang normalnya mustahil dieksploitasi.',
    'For example, when you find reflected XSS in a parameter, it is often unexploitable in practice. This is because modern browsers typically URL-encode the necessary characters when sending the request, and the server doesn\'t decode them. The response that the intended victim receives will merely contain a harmless URL-encoded string.' => 'Browser modern selalu men-URL-encode karakter khusus seperti < dan " sehingga reflected XSS tidak terpicu jika server tidak mendekodenya.',
    'Some caching implementations normalize keyed input when adding it to the cache key. In this case, both of the following requests would have the same key:' => 'Namun jika cache menormalisasi URL saat membangun kunci, dua permintaan berikut memiliki cache key identik:',
    'This behavior can allow you to exploit these otherwise "unexploitable" XSS vulnerabilities. If you send a malicious request using Burp Repeater, you can poison the cache with an unencoded XSS payload. When the victim visits the malicious URL, the payload will still be URL-encoded by their browser; however, once the URL is normalized by the cache, it will have the same cache key as the response containing your unencoded payload.' => 'Anda mengirim payload mentah tanpa URL-encoding untuk meracuni cache, lalu browser korban yang mengirim versi ter-encode tetap menerima balasan beracun karena cache key-nya sama.',
    'As a result, the cache will serve the poisoned response and the payload will be executed client-side. You just need to make sure that the cache is poisoned when the victim visits the URL.' => 'Akibatnya browser korban mengeksekusi payload XSS tersebut saat membuka URL.',
    'Cache key injection' => 'Injeksi cache key',
    'You will sometimes discover a client-side vulnerability in a keyed header. This is also a classic "unexploitable" issue that can sometimes be exploited using cache poisoning.' => 'Terkadang celah sisi klien muncul di header yang masuk ke dalam cache key.',
    "Keyed components are often bundled together in a string to create the cache key. If the cache doesn't implement proper escaping of the delimiters between the components, you can potentially exploit this behavior to craft two different requests that have the same cache key." => 'Jika cache menggabungkan komponen keyed dengan delimiter tanpa escaping, penyerang bisa membuat dua permintaan berbeda dengan cache key persis sama.',
    'The following example uses double-underscores to delimit different components in the cache key and does not escape them. You can exploit this by first poisoning the cache with a request containing your payload in the corresponding keyed header:' => 'Contoh penggunaan pemisah garis bawah ganda pada cache key yang dapat disuntikkan:',
    'If you then induce a victim user to visit the following URL, they would be served the poisoned response:' => 'Saat korban diarahkan ke URL berikut, ia mendapat cache key yang sama persis:',
    'Poisoning internal caches' => 'Meracuni cache internal',
    "So far, we've looked at how you can exploit flaws in the way external web caches are implemented to expose an extended attack surface hidden within seemingly keyed components. However, some websites implement caching behavior directly into the application in addition to using a distinct, external component. This can have several advantages, such as avoiding the kind of parsing discrepancies we looked at earlier." => 'Selain cache eksternal/CDN, aplikasi kadang menyimpan cache terintegrasi di level kode.',
    'As these integrated caches are purpose-built for the specific application, this also gives developers the freedom to tailor their behavior to a greater degree. As a result, these caches can sometimes behave in unusual ways that you wouldn\'t typically see from a more standardized, external cache that needs to be compatible with multiple applications. Sometimes, these strange behaviors can also provide an opportunity for some high-severity cache poisoning exploits.' => 'Cache internal aplikasi sering bekerja tidak lazim dan dapat memicu poisoning berskala sangat luas.',
    'Instead of caching entire responses, some of these caches break the response down into reusable fragments and cache them each separately. For example, a snippet for importing a widely used resource might be stored as a standalone cache entry. Users might then receive a response comprising a mixture of content from the server, as well as several individual fragments from the cache.' => 'Sebagian cache internal memecah halaman menjadi fragmen terpisah (seperti cuplikan impor aset) yang dipakai ulang bersama di berbagai halaman.',
    "As these cached fragments are intended to be reusable across multiple distinct responses, the concept of a cache key doesn't really apply. Every response that contains a given fragment will reuse the same cached fragment, even if the rest of the response is completely different. In a scenario like this, poisoning the cache can have wide-reaching effects, especially if you poison a fragment that is used on every page. As there is no cache key, you would have poisoned every page, for every user, with a single request." => 'Karena fragmen tidak terikat cache key per URL, meracuni satu fragmen saja berdampak ke setiap halaman dan setiap pengguna.',
    'This will often only require you to use basic web cache poisoning techniques, such as manipulating the [[C0]] header.' => 'Biasanya cukup dipicu memakai header klasik seperti [[C0]].',
    'How to identify internal caches' => 'Cara mengidentifikasi cache internal',
    'One of the challenges posed by integrated, application-level caches is that they can be difficult to identify and investigate because there is often no user-facing feedback. To identify these caches, you can look for a few tell-tale signs.' => 'Cache internal jarang menampilkan header diagnostik seperti X-Cache, tetapi dapat dikenali dari gejalanya.',
    'For example, if the response reflects a mixture of both input from the last request you sent and input from a previous request, this is a key indicator that the cache is storing fragments rather than entire responses. The same applies if your input is reflected in responses on multiple distinct pages, in particular on pages in which you never tried to inject your input.' => 'Jika pantulan input dari permintaan sebelumnya muncul di halaman lain tempat Anda tidak mengirim payload, berarti fragmen cache internal aktif.',
    'Other times, the cache\'s behavior may simply be so unusual that the most logical conclusion is that it must be a unique and specialized internal cache.' => 'Perilaku caching yang berbeda antarbagian dalam satu halaman juga menandakan cache fragmen internal.',
    'When a website implements multiple layers of caching, it can make it difficult to comprehend what is happening behind the scenes and understand how the website\'s caching system behaves.' => 'Adanya cache berlapis membuat proses pelacakan memerlukan pengamatan cermat.',
    'Testing internal caches safely' => 'Menguji cache internal dengan aman',
    'When testing ordinary web caches, we recommend using a cache buster to prevent your poisoned response from being served to other users. However, if an integrated cache has no concept of cache keys, then traditional cache busters are useless. This means that it\'s very easy to accidentally poison the cache for genuine users.' => 'Karena fragmen internal tidak memakai cache key, cache buster tidak mencegah dampak ke pengguna lain.',
    'Therefore, it is important that you do your best to mitigate the potential damage when testing these kinds of vulnerabilities. Think carefully about the effect of your injected payload before sending each request. In particular, you should make sure that you only poison the cache using a domain that you control, rather than some arbitrary "[[C0]]". This way, you are in control of what happens next if something goes wrong.' => 'Gunakan hanya domain kendali Anda sendiri saat menguji (jangan memakai domain contoh sembarang seperti "[[C0]]").',
];
